255
00:18:33,660 --> 00:18:37,307
So please, until we're done, you
must stay out of the factory.

256
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:39,820
Don't even come close. Roger!

257
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,240
And no peeking.

258
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:43,577
I don't care who you are
or what you might need.

259
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:46,360
I want absolute privacy. Roger!

260
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:48,940
You won't hear a peek, Lady Patty!

261
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:52,420
You're so sweet. Thank you.

262
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:56,420
The whole island's cheering
for you! Good luck!

263
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,540
Good, now they won't see Sanji,

264
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:03,528
but dealing with the chefs will
be a little more complicated.

265
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:08,080
Chefs, please come inside one by one.

266
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:17,852
Beach, head chef of the first
kitchen, reporting for duty.

267
00:19:24,820 --> 00:19:26,740
This should only take a sec

268
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:31,937
I'm just giving your memories a little...

269
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:32,850
edit

270
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:35,100
Could you let me down?

271
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:37,220
Okay, here you go

272
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:39,660
Bumpy ride?

273
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,257
No time to complain.

274
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:44,977
I drew a diagram of the wedding cake
on the way here to speed things up.

275
00:19:45,060 --> 00:19:45,890
What?

276
00:19:45,973 --> 00:19:46,803
You remember it?

277
00:19:46,886 --> 00:19:47,997
Well, it's close enough.

278
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:52,117
That's crazy—the design is one
thing, but how do you know?

279
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:53,030
The ingredients without

280
00:19:53,113 --> 00:19:53,943
ever tasting

281
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:54,856
it by

282
00:19:54,939 --> 00:20:01,017
its scent.

283
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:05,057
This guy now—let's hurry up!

284
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:06,277
Every last second counts.

285
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:07,320
second counts

286
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:11,138
Y 'all's a pudding!

287
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:13,339
That chef outfit looks cute on you!

288
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:19,557
Don't tell me Lady Pudding is not already!

289
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:20,597
What a good husband.

290
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:22,540
Here to help. Huh? Me?

291
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,577
I edited the memories of the chefs,

292
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:28,937
so they don't know about
the whole wedding fiasco.

293
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:33,961
They think it went off without a hitch,
which would mean we're husband and wife now.

294
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,129
You know, happy as can be.

295
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:42,780
So this story is, the wedding cake was
ruined due to some unexpected weather.

296
00:20:43,300 --> 00:20:47,637
Mama got angry, that's the same, so we
have to make the cake all over again.

297
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:50,191
Don't contradict their new memories, okay?

298
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:51,300
No problem.

299
00:20:51,540 --> 00:20:54,577
The memories of when they made
the original cake are still fresh.

300
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:58,417
So with all of them here to help, we
should be able to reproduce it accurately.

301
00:20:58,500 --> 00:20:59,330
Whoa!

302
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:00,590
Huh?

303
00:21:00,673 --> 00:21:03,340
Who came up with this
diagram for the wedding cake?

304
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:05,677
And a recipe, too? That'd be me.

305
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:09,160
You sketched this out on
the way over here? Uh-huh.

306
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:11,678
Let me know if there's any mistakes.

307
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:12,918
Are you kidding me?

308
00:21:13,100 --> 00:21:16,477
This recipe is immaculate all
the way down to the secret

309
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:19,517
ingredient Executive Chef Struzan's
been awake coming up with.

310
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:22,188
I heard you were skilled,
but I had no clue.

311
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:23,673
You are brilliant, sir.

312
00:21:23,880 --> 00:21:26,780
Two newlywed chefs making
their own wedding cake.

313
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:29,220
Romantic, huh? Newlywed?

314
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:33,756
Quite the unusual situation, but you
might as well make the best of it.

315
00:21:34,380 --> 00:21:35,740
Don't embarrass me.

316
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:36,780
I'm shy.

317
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:40,820
Sanji, your wife fainted!

318
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:43,180
His wife? Your wife!

319
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:45,160
Your wife! Your wife!

320
00:21:45,820 --> 00:21:46,660
Sanji, sir!

321
00:21:46,860 --> 00:21:47,877
Come help your wife!

322
00:21:47,960 --> 00:21:48,790
Stop it!

323
00:21:48,873 --> 00:21:49,703
You're killing her!

324
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:54,760
I really think gross!
I think gross! Get up!

325
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:56,150
What?

326
00:21:56,233 --> 00:21:57,417
Now he's bossing me around?

327
00:21:57,500 --> 00:21:59,937
Well, I like a man who
knows what he wants.

328
00:22:00,020 --> 00:22:02,477
If he needs to wear the pants
in our relationship, then...

329
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:05,160
You know, mutual respect
is very important.

330
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:11,260
Hey, you talk down to me like that again,
and I swear I will skin your ass, Sanji.

331
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:13,100
So here's what I need.

332
00:22:13,280 --> 00:22:16,420
Some non-homogenized milk,
sugar beets, and bananas.

333
00:22:16,700 --> 00:22:19,620
Also black sesame seeds,
soy flour, and yogurt.

334
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:21,280
As much as you can get.

335
00:22:21,540 --> 00:22:22,380
Yes, sir!

336
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:27,860
Listen up.

337
00:22:28,040 --> 00:22:31,334
This job is life or death,
and it's a race against time.

338
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:35,691
Chiffon, get baking on that
giant chiffon cake immediately.

339
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:41,188
Pudding, you start tempering the chocolate
and make sure we have enough of it.

340
00:22:41,380 --> 00:22:44,497
I'm setting the cook time at
two hours and forty minutes.

341
00:22:44,580 --> 00:22:47,717
You weren't kidding when you
called this a race against time.

342
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:51,660
Once everything else is done,
I'll add my secret ingredient.

343
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:56,000
It'll bring boundless
joy to whoever tastes it.

344
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:58,580
It's the essence of true sweetness.

345
00:22:59,980 --> 00:23:02,440
Wow, the essence of true sweetness, huh?

346
00:23:03,220 --> 00:23:04,455
In about three hours,

347
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:08,717
we'll load the partially done cake on
a ship and depart from Cacao Island.

348
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:12,624
After it cools down a bit, we'll
decorate it while we're sailing.

349
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:15,637
Big Mom and the Sunny
should be heading our way,

350
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:17,437
and by the time they intercept us,

351
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:21,580
we'll have the greatest cake ever
made waiting for them. I see.

352
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:23,177
That sounds very efficient.

353
00:23:23,260 --> 00:23:24,090
I don't know.

354
00:23:24,173 --> 00:23:25,357
That pace is going to be murder.

355
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:28,240
I think it's impossible,
actually. Quiet, you!

356
00:23:28,580 --> 00:23:30,997
We'll do it because the
alternative is dead!

357
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:34,727
In that case, we shall strive
to make the impossible possible!

358
00:23:35,360 --> 00:23:36,280
All right.

359
00:23:37,060 --> 00:23:38,600
Time to start baking.

360
00:23:40,500 --> 00:23:43,020
They saved Lola and I'll save them.

361
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:45,740
I have to protect Sanji.

362
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:47,440
Just you wait.

363
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:52,308
This chiffon cake is going to be so
fluffy it'll bring the world to its knees!

364
00:23:52,620 --> 00:23:55,032
This is the sweet chocolate of salvation.

365
00:23:55,720 --> 00:23:58,180
Chocolate that will change fate itself.

366
00:23:59,700 --> 00:24:02,053
Hang on just a little bit longer, Luffy.

367
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:05,540
I'll show them what I'm made of.

368
00:24:05,820 --> 00:24:07,240
My chef spirit.

369
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:13,600
Katakuri, it's me.

370
00:24:13,860 --> 00:24:16,140
Escaped from the jaws of death, Press.

371
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:17,900
By the skin of my tongue.

372
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:20,920
They really put on a sorry show.

373
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:24,100
Pedro licked the bucket.

374
00:24:24,860 --> 00:24:28,140
Hey, Straw Hat, you saw it, didn't you?

375
00:24:29,660 --> 00:24:36,317
He tried to sacrifice his worthless life
in some pathetic attempt to kill me,

376
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:38,317
but I'm still lickety living.

377
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:44,237
As you can see in other words, his
death was utterly lickety meaningless,

378
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:48,037
and you're going to die
in vain—just like he did.

379
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:51,737
So you just lickety lie there
and meet your maker quietly!

380
00:24:51,820 --> 00:24:56,397
Why don't you and Straw Hats
underlings they escaped our

381
00:24:56,480 --> 00:24:59,377
encirclement by launching
their damned ship into the sky?

382
00:24:59,460 --> 00:25:04,437
Mama and I are chasing them down at this
very moment, taking a stroll on the waves.

383
00:25:04,520 --> 00:25:09,737
They're trying their best to escape,
but we'll catch up, lickety split!

384
00:25:09,820 --> 00:25:10,650
split

385
00:25:11,340 --> 00:25:13,940
Amon's fleet will be here soon as well.

386
00:25:16,400 --> 00:25:17,800
Hey, Barrel.

387
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:22,360
Oh, Katakuri.

388
00:25:22,820 --> 00:25:24,644
You can rest when this is over.

389
00:25:24,900 --> 00:25:27,782
Our soldiers can't go
anywhere if you're napping.

390
00:25:28,320 --> 00:25:29,150
Right.

391
00:25:29,233 --> 00:25:32,453
Straw Hat thought he was taking
a stand to save his crew.

392
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:37,400
Barrel, round up some of the soldiers
and set fire to Straw Hat's ship.

393
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:38,740
With pleasure.

394
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:40,230
Good news!

395
00:25:40,313 --> 00:25:42,597
We found a mirror that
links to the ship's locker.

396
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:43,621
It's right here.

397
00:25:43,900 --> 00:25:46,017
There's more where that came from, too!

398
00:25:46,100 --> 00:25:50,257
A couple of flaming arrows straight
through the mirror room should do the job.

399
00:25:50,340 --> 00:25:53,317
And while they're scrambling
to deal with the fire,

400
00:25:53,400 --> 00:25:56,341
Mama will smash those rats
into itty-bitty pieces.

401
00:25:57,900 --> 00:25:59,020
What the...

402
00:26:03,080 --> 00:26:04,880
Hand over that mirror!

403
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:07,640
Don't lay a finger on my crew!

404
00:26:09,140 --> 00:26:12,880
Are we having a one-on-one
duel or not, Straw Hat?

405
00:26:14,620 --> 00:26:15,840
Suck on that!

406
00:26:20,220 --> 00:26:25,200
Now, let's burn down that ship
before someone interrupts us again.

407
00:26:26,580 --> 00:26:27,410
Roger!

408
00:26:30,700 --> 00:26:33,180
I'll laugh if you miss, Choscar.

409
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:34,980
Is that a joke, Moscar?

410
00:26:41,640 --> 00:26:42,470
Hurry!

411
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:44,460
Fire!

412
00:26:47,840 --> 00:26:49,920
Stop it!

413
00:27:00,020 --> 00:27:03,040
Stay away! Hey!

414
00:27:03,420 --> 00:27:04,320
Same to you.

415
00:27:06,460 --> 00:27:09,257
Those are my little siblings
you're trying to attack.

416
00:27:09,340 --> 00:27:10,620
Leave them alone.

417
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:19,720
You're a piece.

418
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:25,420
Hey, it's me!

419
00:27:29,020 --> 00:27:30,640
Nami, Chimpe, anyone!

420
00:27:31,340 --> 00:27:32,380
Can you hear me?

421
00:27:47,820 --> 00:27:49,920
Hey, can you hear me?

422
00:27:50,180 --> 00:27:51,380
Is that Ruthie?

423
00:27:51,640 --> 00:27:52,760
The mirror!

424
00:27:54,360 --> 00:27:56,580
Hey, I'm here. What's wrong?

425
00:27:56,880 --> 00:28:00,100
I need you to find all our mirrors. What?

426
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:03,100
Like in the bathroom or locker room? Huh?

427
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:09,020
Burn! Burn! Burn!

428
00:28:09,800 --> 00:28:12,500
Ready for another one? Of course!

429
00:28:12,820 --> 00:28:13,780
Waiting on you!

430
00:28:16,160 --> 00:28:17,440
Burn! Burn!

431
00:28:20,280 --> 00:28:21,110
Luffy!

432
00:28:21,220 --> 00:28:22,573
What about the mirrors?

433
00:28:22,660 --> 00:28:24,760
Break them all! To pieces!

434
00:28:25,100 --> 00:28:26,457
Are you out of your mind?

435
00:28:26,540 --> 00:28:27,977
Then how will you get back?

436
00:28:28,060 --> 00:28:29,457
That was the whole plan!

437
00:28:29,540 --> 00:28:30,920
Don't worry about me!

438
00:28:31,160 --> 00:28:32,513
We'll get through this!

439
00:28:33,740 --> 00:28:35,152
I'll work something out.

440
00:28:36,980 --> 00:28:37,810
What's that?

441
00:28:39,860 --> 00:28:40,919
I smell something.

442
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:43,631
Even though I don't have a nose, Yo-Ho-Ho.

443
00:28:48,860 --> 00:28:50,340
The room's on fire!

444
00:28:51,540 --> 00:28:52,370
What's wrong?

445
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:55,536
How did this happen?

446
00:28:57,740 --> 00:28:58,570
What?

447
00:28:58,653 --> 00:28:59,540
What?!

448
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:07,140
Flaming arrows from the mirror, cannon
shots from behind, one king after another!

449
00:29:07,360 --> 00:29:11,517
If I had eyes in my sockets, I assure
you they would be spinning right now!

450
00:29:11,600 --> 00:29:12,430
Focus!

451
00:29:12,513 --> 00:29:13,692
Let's put that fire out!

452
00:29:15,820 --> 00:29:17,320
Good. Again.

453
00:29:17,620 --> 00:29:18,540
More arrows.

454
00:29:18,940 --> 00:29:21,020
You heard Barrel, Joscar.

455
00:29:21,440 --> 00:29:24,120
More arrows for fire, Pascar!

456
00:29:24,360 --> 00:29:26,420
You two cut it out! That's enough!

457
00:29:31,660 --> 00:29:32,740
You okay?

458
00:29:33,200 --> 00:29:34,820
Hey, are you alright?

459
00:29:35,740 --> 00:29:37,120
Wee-hee-hee.

460
00:29:37,620 --> 00:29:39,600
We're going to storm the ship.

461
00:29:39,800 --> 00:29:40,859
Is everyone ready?

462
00:29:41,260 --> 00:29:43,360
Rawr! Rawr! Rawr!

463
00:29:43,500 --> 00:29:44,600
Damn you!

464
00:29:45,640 --> 00:29:46,470
Aaaaaah!

465
00:29:52,220 --> 00:29:53,800
Nami! Go!

466
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:56,977
Break the mirrors! Hurry! But...

467
00:29:57,060 --> 00:29:59,460
They're sending an army to attack you!

468
00:29:59,660 --> 00:30:00,940
I can't stop them!

469
00:30:01,080 --> 00:30:01,920
I'm too busy!

470
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:05,460
It'll take all I've got to
beat the guy I'm fighting!

471
00:30:16,140 --> 00:30:16,970
Hey!

472
00:30:17,180 --> 00:30:18,197
This looks bad!

473
00:30:18,280 --> 00:30:19,620
It's too close!

474
00:30:25,140 --> 00:30:26,780
We can't escape!

475
00:30:31,300 --> 00:30:32,620
Are you there?

476
00:30:44,480 --> 00:30:46,860
Luffy, I'm sorry.

477
00:30:49,700 --> 00:30:51,940
I've got you now.

478
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:54,080
Tommy, what's wrong?

479
00:30:55,780 --> 00:30:59,380
I think this might be it for us.
